contrib/pgbench/README

pgbench Extension Developer Notes
=================================

Overview
--------
The `contrib/pgbench` extension exposes the shared statistical distributions,
hashes, domain permutations, TPC-C NURand / syllable / string generators,
calendar date arithmetic, and array generators from `src/common/pgbench_funcs.c`
as SQL-callable functions in the `pgbench` schema.

Architecture
------------
- `contrib/pgbench/pgbench.c` provides thin `PG_FUNCTION_INFO_V1` wrappers
  around `src/common/pgbench_funcs.c`.
- Session PRNG state is stored in `static pg_prng_state pgbench_ext_prng_state`
  and lazily seeded on first use if `pgbench.setseed()` has not been called.
- Session-sticky NURand `C` constants for the standard TPC-C `A` domains
  (`255`, `1023`, `8191`, and fallback) are maintained per backend session
  and reset whenever `pgbench.setseed()` is invoked.
- `pgbench.format_string(text, VARIADIC "any")` inspects argument OIDs via
  `get_fn_expr_argtype()` and converts arbitrary SQL types when needed using
  `getTypeOutputInfo()` / `OidOutputFunctionCall()`.

Adding a New Function
---------------------
1. Implement the frontend/backend-safe algorithm in `src/common/pgbench_funcs.c`
   and declare it in `src/include/common/pgbench_funcs.h`.
2. Add the `PG_FUNCTION_INFO_V1` wrapper in `contrib/pgbench/pgbench.c`.
3. Register the SQL signature in `contrib/pgbench/pgbench--1.0.sql`.
4. Add regression tests in `contrib/pgbench/sql/pgbench.sql` and update
   `contrib/pgbench/expected/pgbench.out`.
5. Document the SQL function in `doc/src/sgml/pgbench-ext.sgml`.
